; A synchronous exception on `baremetal-aarch64`, taken on purpose: a
; 32-bit volatile load from an address one byte past a 16-byte-aligned
; block. `_start` sets SCTLR_EL1.A, so a misaligned access is an
; alignment fault on the arena's Normal memory (QEMU enforces it,
; measured: ESR_EL1 0x96000021 - EC 0x25, a data abort at the current
; exception level, DFSC 0x21, alignment).
;
; `scripts/check-embedded.sh` A12 boots it under QEMU `virt` and
; requires the boot line, then the fault report the vector table writes
; - the vector offset (0x200, "current EL, SPx, synchronous"), ESR_EL1,
; the faulting instruction's address (ELR_EL1) and the faulting data
; address (FAR_EL1) - and exit status 81, docs/memory-model.md
; MM-EXEC-16's row for an unhandled CPU exception. Before the vector
; table existed the same program spun until the gate's timeout killed
; it: a fault was a hang, and nothing said which instruction.
;
; The raw primitive: this probe is about what the CPU does when nothing
; refused the access first.
(import IO)
(import Mem)

(:: misaligned (-> Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (misaligned a)
  (__vload32 (+ a 1)))

(:: main Int)
;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  {
    (println "FAULT PROBE")
    (println (misaligned (memAlloc 16)))
    (println "NOT REACHED")
    0
  })
